@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Virtual-call refinement lattice and assumptions

skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFC
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #495057
  RoundCorner 12
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F1F3F5
  BorderColor #495057
}

rectangle "CHA\nall represented compatible\nconcrete runtime types\nconfidence 0.75" as CHA #74C0FC
rectangle "RTA\nCHA ∩ represented\nallocated types\nconfidence 0.80" as RTA #FFF3BF
rectangle "VTA\nRTA ∩ receiver-reaching\nallocation types\nconfidence 0.85" as VTA #FFE8CC
rectangle "sorted dispatch targets\nown override, otherwise\ninherited/default methods" as TARGET #D3F9D8
rectangle "out-of-graph record\n0 → none\n1 → singleton target\nmany → ambiguous" as RESULT #D3F9D8

CHA -down-> RTA : add closed-world\nallocation assumption
RTA -down-> VTA : add receiver DFG\nassignment assumption
CHA ..> TARGET : <latex>T_{CHA}</latex>
RTA ..> TARGET : <latex>T_{RTA} \subseteq T_{CHA}</latex>
VTA ..> TARGET : <latex>T_{VTA} \subseteq T_{RTA}</latex>
TARGET --> RESULT

note right of CHA
  Broadest represented target set.
  Use when allocations are incomplete.
end note

note right of VTA
  Narrowest mode here, but not a
  full points-to or runtime proof.
end note

note bottom of RESULT
  No mode adds, removes, or relabels CPG edges.
  Missing libraries, reflection, and dynamic loading
  remain outside the represented closed world.
end note

legend bottom
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#74C0FC>| hierarchy compatibility |
|<#FFF3BF>| global allocation evidence |
|<#FFE8CC>| receiver-reaching assignment evidence |
|<#D3F9D8>| deterministic immutable target evidence |
endlegend
@enduml
